  "caption": "Quinn spent six months out injured, passed the tests, and still froze on the first quick turn at training. Legs ready, brain not so sure.\n\nThat's common. Trust often comes back after strength does, because months of protecting a limb can teach the brain to be cautious. Confidence tends to grow from evidence rather than time alone.\n\nWhat may help: strength and hop tests against the other side, reintroducing feared moves slow then fast then unplanned, practising the movement that caused the injury in small steps, and returning in stages. Your first game may feel harder than training, and that's normal.\n\nNew or worsening pain or swelling is worth checking. If fear or low mood is weighing on you, talk to your GP.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
